  "limitations": [
    "This report describes client-observed behavior for one endpoint configuration, not model capability.",
    "Metrics are reported with AIPerf's own units; denominator changes invalidate comparison.",
    "Token counts come from provider-reported usage, so the throughput denominator is authoritative for the served model. No independent client tokenizer ran, so client-versus-provider agreement was not observed. Workload sizing is instead checked as provider-versus-target conformance against the profile's requested input size.",
    "20 of 20 completed trials (100%) stopped at the configured output ceiling (`finish_reason: length`). Those trials did not finish naturally, so `request_latency` is a right-censored lower bound on time-to-completion and is marked as censored. Time-to-first-token is unaffected. Success counters exclude these trials and report them as `truncated_trials`.",
    "19 completed trial(s) spent the entire completion budget on provider-reported reasoning tokens and emitted no visible answer content. Output throughput in this run describes reasoning-token emission, not answer generation.",
    "Cache-write counts are not exposed by AIPerf 0.13.0 as a metric. They were recovered from the raw streamed `usage.prompt_tokens_details.created_cache_tokens` field and are labelled with that source. Cache-read counts come from AIPerf's normalized `usage_prompt_cache_read_tokens` metric."
  ],
